enemy_spawns = Array[Vector2i]([Vector2i(1, 1), Vector2i(24, 1), Vector2i(1, 10), Vector2i(24, 10), Vector2i(13, 6)])
; The duct idea taken as far as it goes: a lattice of shuttle rails with no cover anywhere in it.
; Everything in this room can see everything else from the moment the door shuts, and almost none of
; it can go straight at anything. It is the most restrictive floor on the level and the most open
; sightline, at the same time, which is a combination the game has not had a room for.
;
; It is also the room the floor's two enemies were waiting for. The Load Balancer is answered by
; getting inside about a hundred pixels and going round it, and here the rails decide which way
; round is even available — the fight becomes a question about the geometry rather than about the
; angle. The Stale Replica walks the route the player walked, and a route through a lattice is a
; route that comes back at them along a line they picked themselves. Neither needed a line of code
; for either; both fall out of the ground having a shape.
;
; No obstacles at all, deliberately, and for `data_grid_floor`'s reason turned inside out: that room
; removes cover so the only question is where you stand, and this one removes cover so the only
; question is how you get there.
ducts = Array[Rect2i]([Rect2i(3, 2, 5, 1), Rect2i(10, 2, 6, 1), Rect2i(18, 2, 5, 1), Rect2i(3, 9, 5, 1), Rect2i(10, 9, 6, 1), Rect2i(18, 9, 5, 1), Rect2i(7, 4, 1, 4), Rect2i(18, 4, 1, 4), Rect2i(11, 4, 1, 2), Rect2i(14, 6, 1, 2)])
thermal_zones = Array[Rect2i]([Rect2i(8, 4, 3, 4), Rect2i(15, 4, 3, 4)])
reward_spawn = Vector2i(13, 6)
difficulty = 3
